# AP News - removed, not broken-and-left.
# The feeds.apnews.com/apf-* endpoints AP retired returned nothing; their
# apnews.com/hub/*.rss successors returned nothing either. Two guesses, two
# empty feeds, and AP publishes no documented public RSS to guess a third time
# from. Reuters is the same story - it withdrew its public news feeds. Wire
# coverage comes from the Guardian and the BBC below, both of which answer.

# The Guardian
# Added for pictures as much as for coverage: the Guardian is the one source
# here that puts an image on essentially every item in its RSS, where
# Bloomberg, the FT and the Economist put none and block the build from
# reading their pages.
https://www.theguardian.com/uk/business/rss "~Guardian Business" guardian finance
https://www.theguardian.com/world/rss "~Guardian World" guardian news

# BBC News
# BBC ships no enclosures either, but unlike the financial press it answers the
# build, so scripts/harvest_images.py resolves an og:image for roughly five in
# six of its stories.
https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/business/rss.xml "~BBC Business" bbc finance

